# Normalise line endings on the way in, so a checkout on any platform is consistent and a
# diff never shows a whole file as changed because somebody's editor rewrote the endings.
* text=auto

# Files that must keep LF whatever the platform. The git hooks are shell scripts and the
# workflows are read by a Linux runner; CRLF breaks both.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Files that must keep CRLF, on every platform including a Linux runner. The .editorconfig
# rule for C# says CRLF and `dotnet format --verify-no-changes` enforces it, so leaving these
# to `text=auto` would mean the format gate passes on Windows and fails wherever the checkout
# produced LF. Pinning them here makes the two agree by construction rather than by luck.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cs text eol=crlf
*.csproj text eol=crlf
*.props text eol=crlf
*.slnx text eol=crlf

# Binary, never diffed and never converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
